+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Browser-only defects pinned this leg (from the fixed external Cypress acceptance suite)
+
+Both defects are app-side. Captain MUST NOT edit `js/` or `index.html`; Crew fixes from the specs below and QM builds the checker.
+
+1. **List re-render replaces item nodes.** `render()` sets `todoList.innerHTML`, so every item's `<li>` is detached and re-created on any state change (item toggle, toggle-all, clear-completed). A real browser that holds a node reference across the click sees it detached (Cypress `cy.eq()` / `cy.find()` detached-from-DOM errors: "mark all as completed", "clear the complete state of all items", "mark items as complete", "un-mark items as complete").
+   - Pinned by source-level conformance, not a DOM-behaviour scenario: happy-dom re-queries by title and cannot reproduce the chain-break, so a behaviour scenario would pass green against the bug. `scantlings/todo-dom-identity.md` rules DI-1 / DI-2 name the checker contract; the checker parses `js/app.js` and flags any single-item or toggle-all/clear-completed path that reaches a `todoList.innerHTML` rebuild instead of in-place mutation.
+   - The fix preserves the existing node: toggle the `completed` class and the `.toggle` `checked` in place, do not rebuild the list.
+
+2. **Editing does not hide other controls.** No stylesheet rule hides `.view` while `.editing`, so the toggle stays visible during edit (Cypress `expected '<input.toggle>' not to be 'visible'`). happy-dom has no layout, so this is browser-only and guarded by the same source-level conformance check.
+   - Pinned by `scantlings/todo-dom-identity.md` rule EV-1: the checker inspects the stylesheet carried by `index.html` (inline `<style>` and any linked `css/app.css`) for a `.todo-list li.editing .view` hide rule. The fix ships that rule.
+
+## Watchbill
+
+`watchbill.json` `watch1` carries the single conformance scenario above. It reddens against the current code (rebuild + missing CSS rule) and goes green once Crew preserves node identity and ships the editing-hide rule, and QM's checker discharges the scantling.
+
+## Decision
+
+Authored specs + scantling + watchbill only. No production code, no edits under `js/` or `index.html`, no commit. Next leg: QM implements the source-level conformance checker in verification support; Crew fixes the render path and the editing stylesheet from the specs.
