+# Todo list item DOM-identity and editing-visibility scantling
+
+This scantling fixes the mechanical shape of the TodoMVC list render and edit
+behaviour. A SOURCE-LEVEL conformance checker (QM-owned verification support)
+discharges it against `js/app.js` and the shipped stylesheet carried by
+`index.html` (its inline `<style>` and any linked stylesheet such as
+`css/app.css`). The current build violates every rule below; each rule names the
+observed acceptance-suite failure it closes.
+
+## DI-1: Item-state changes must mutate the existing node, not rebuild the list
+
+When a single todo's `completed` value changes (by its own checkbox toggle, or by
+toggle-all), the app MUST NOT detach and re-create that todo's `<li>` element. The
+same `HTMLLIElement` instance attached to `.todo-list` before the change MUST
+remain attached afterwards. Re-rendering the whole list by replacing
+`todoList.innerHTML` in response to an item-state change is forbidden.
+
+Conformance: a source-level checker parses `js/app.js` and asserts that every
+single-item state-change path reaches in-place mutation of the existing `<li>`
+rather than a full-list rebuild. The checked paths are the handler invoked when a
+`.toggle` checkbox changes and the toggle-all handler. A path violates DI-1 when
+it can reach an assignment to `todoList.innerHTML` (or any equivalent full-list
+teardown) for a single-item state change, instead of toggling the `<li>`'s
+`completed` class and the `.toggle` `checked` state on the live node. The current
+`render()` assigns `todoList.innerHTML` and each checked path calls it, so the
+build violates DI-1. Closes acceptance failures "should allow me to mark items as
+complete" and "should allow me to un-mark items as complete" (the `cy.find()`
+detached-from-DOM errors).
+
+## DI-2: Toggle-all and clear-completed must preserve surviving nodes
+
+After toggle-all (mark or clear) or clear-completed, every `<li>` that remains in
+the list MUST be the same node instance that was present before the action. A node
+is removed only when the todo itself is removed (destroy, or clear-completed that
+drops it). Rebuilding the list on these actions is forbidden for surviving nodes.
+
+Conformance: a source-level checker parses `js/app.js` and asserts that the
+toggle-all and clear-completed paths preserve every surviving `<li>` by mutating
+it in place, not by reassigning `todoList.innerHTML`. A path violates DI-2 when it
+rebuilds the list for nodes that survive the action. The current `render()`
+rebuilds the whole list, so these paths violate DI-2. Closes acceptance failures
+"should allow me to mark all items as completed" and "should allow me to clear the
+complete state of all items" (the `cy.eq()` detached-from-DOM errors).
+
+## EV-1: Editing must hide the item's other controls
+
+The shipped stylesheet MUST contain a rule that, while a `.todo-list li` carries the
+class `editing`, hides its `.view` block (and therefore its `.toggle` checkbox, its
+`label`, and its `.destroy` button) and shows its `.edit` input. A bare
+data-attribute toggle is not enough; the control must be visually hidden so a
+visibility probe reports it not visible.
+
+Conformance: a source-level checker inspects the shipped stylesheet carried by
+`index.html` (its inline `<style>` and any linked stylesheet such as
+`css/app.css`) and asserts a rule matching `.todo-list li.editing .view` (or an
+equivalent selector that removes `.view` from layout, for example `display:none`
+or `visibility:hidden`) exists, and that `.toggle` is not left visible while
+editing. The current build links no stylesheet and ships no such rule, so it
+violates EV-1. Closes acceptance failure "should hide other controls when
+editing" (the `expected '<input.toggle>' not to be 'visible'` assertion).
